From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: preserve resource failures and retry failed votes

Do not cache a failed interconnect request as accepted bandwidth. Bulk
votes may fail after a partial update; invalidate the bandwidth cache so
the next request always retries. A close request must not skip a retry.

Check the final OPP rate result before presets/interrupt enable and
unwind hardware, controller and interconnect resources on failure.
Retain the actual resume errno after the existing cleanup paths instead
of replacing every failure with EBUSY.

Compared against current upstream f47d223627f80cb7a1eb14c585fe6cb35de5e984,
which retains these paths. This inactive source candidate does not match
or activate Uke hardware. Actual-function host fault fixtures cover each
resource stage and GCC/Clang builds retain existing success behavior.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_resources.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_resources.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_resources.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_resources.c
@@ -37,12 +37,15 @@
 
 			core->icc_tbl[i].avg_bw = bw_kbps;
 
-			core->power.icc_bw = bw_kbps;
 			break;
 		}
 	}
 
-	return icc_bulk_set_bw(core->icc_count, core->icc_tbl);
+	ret = icc_bulk_set_bw(core->icc_count, core->icc_tbl);
+	/* A failed bulk vote can be partial; force the next request to retry. */
+	core->power.icc_bw = ret ? 0 : bw_kbps;
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 int iris_unset_icc_bw(struct iris_core *core)
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
@@ -483,7 +483,9 @@
 	freq = core->power.clk_freq ? core->power.clk_freq :
 				      (u32)ULONG_MAX;
 
-	iris_opp_set_rate(core->dev, freq);
+	ret = iris_opp_set_rate(core->dev, freq);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_power_off_hw;
 
 	iris_vpu_set_preset_registers(core);
 
@@ -493,6 +495,8 @@
 
 	return 0;
 
+err_power_off_hw:
+	core->iris_platform_data->vpu_ops->power_off_hw(core);
 err_power_off_ctrl:
 	core->iris_platform_data->vpu_ops->power_off_controller(core);
 err_unvote_icc:
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_common.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_common.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_common.c
@@ -176,5 +176,5 @@
 error:
 	dev_err(core->dev, "failed to resume\n");
 
-	return -EBUSY;
+	return ret;
 }
